  <data name="ReadMeTextBox" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>DWS 11 (Destroy Windows 11 Spying) removes spying and telemetry from Windows 11. It also runs on Windows 7, 8/8.1 and 10.

What it does:
- Detects your Windows version. Windows 11 has its own options panel.
- Disables telemetry services. It does not delete them by default; deleting them is an expert option.
- Disables spying scheduled tasks.
- Blocks telemetry domains in the HOSTS file. The Windows firewall is never touched.
- Removes Metro/UWP apps by exact package name, for all users and provisioned copies. On Windows 11: Copilot, Teams, the new Outlook, Clipchamp, Widgets and more.
- Applies Windows 11 registry settings: Copilot, Recall, Widgets, and Start/Explorer ads.
- Windows 11 dark theme that follows the system accent colour.

A registry backup (55 values) is saved before every run. Restore it with "Restaurar copia..." or make one now with "Hacer copia ahora".

WARNING: removing Metro apps is permanent and cannot be undone. Some changes are not reverted by the registry backup alone. Create a system restore point before running the program.

Compared with the original version, the HTTP auto-update and the firewall rules for explorer.exe and WSearch were removed, because they broke the Store, Windows Update and Explorer.

Credits: original project Destroy-Windows-10-Spying. This version: https://github.com/Akunimal/Destroy-Windows-11-Revival

Command-line arguments:
/lang= - program language. Example: /lang=en
/deleteapp= - removes one Metro app from Windows. Example: /deleteapp=bing or /deleteapp=note
/destroy - runs the spyware removal.
IMPORTANT: /destroy and /deleteapp= cannot be combined, and /deleteapp= cannot be repeated.</value>
